    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0997" n="1505" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/10–2248: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of State, at Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-22T17:00:00-05:00">October 22, 1948—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Telmar 91. Personal for Marshall and Rusk
                    from Lovett. Re Martel 73,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d691-f1"/> reaction of White House so strong against action
                    suggested in Delga 432,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d691-f2"/> with specific prohibition against paragraph (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) and most reluctant and qualified acceptance
                    paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), there is no chance of getting
                    decision reversed. Our Telmar 86<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d691-f3"/> was merely playing for a break in hopes Secretary’s Greek
                    trip may have disclosed facts which might help affirmative presentation.</p>
                <p>We agree any cover plan would be transparent and can only hope Arab bloc and
                    other countries supporting postponement may continue take the lead. Postponement
                    appears increasingly important if problem is to be dealt with realistically on
                    its merits and outside domestic politics.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
